            <div xml:id="d548">

                <pb facs="0687" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-25T12:00:00+01:00">April 25,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 25—7:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. Paragraph 1 of the Department’s 87, April 20, 5 p.m., was orally conveyed to
                    Chief of Far Eastern Division, Foreign Office, who duly expressed his
                    appreciation.</p>
                <p>As regards paragraph 2 (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Foreign Office stated
                    that when the selection of a financial expert, as explained by Fisher to
                    Atherton, is determined he will be attached to the British Legation in Peiping.
                    Paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Foreign Office has received no reply
                    from Japanese or any other Government. Paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >c</hi>) Foreign Office stated that this question “is being handled informally
                    by Fisher and not in the usual way” but the position of the British Government
                    is clearly set forth in the note written by Fisher<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d548-f1"/> (forwarded with Embassy’s despatch No. 1365, April 12)
                    copies of which have been handed to Japanese and French representatives.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
